{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>On the first day of the first month, on the first of the month, you shall set up the Tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting</b> — According to the opinion of our Sages (Sifra, end of parashat Tzav, siman 291, and elsewhere) that this is the eighth day of the ordination (milu'im), the sense of the verse is that you shall set up the Tabernacle and it shall stand thus permanently, and you shall not take it down, nor shall you set it up again, for when the camps journeyed, the Levites would take it down and set it up. There was no need to command now concerning the setting up of the first seven days, for He had already said to him initially, <i>\"והקמת את המשכן כמשפטו אשר הראית בהר\"</i> (Exodus 26:30), and since He now specified to him that on the first day of the month its erection would be permanent, he understood that during the seven days of ordination he would need to erect and take it down. And perhaps this was so in order to train the Levites in its work, for from him they would see and so they would do, or it was to crown the day with this crown.<br>And according to their opinion, it appears that during the first seven days he would set it up each morning, and it would stand thus all day and all night, and at dawn he would take it down and immediately set it up again, for the verse says <i>\"ופתח אהל מועד תשבו יומם ולילה\"</i> (Leviticus 8:35), and there is no entrance to the tent except at the time of its erection. And they have already interpreted (Sifra, Leviticus 1:5) <i>\"אל פתח אהל מועד\"</i> — at the time when it is open and not at the time when it is disassembled. And they said (Zevachim 55a) that shelamim offerings slaughtered before the doors of the Temple were opened are invalid, as it is stated (Leviticus 3:2) <i>\"ושחטו פתח אהל מועד\"</i> — at the time when it is open and not when it is locked, and likewise in the Tabernacle — before the Levites set up the Tabernacle, and after the Levites disassembled the Tabernacle, they are invalid. Furthermore, he would offer on it the constant offering (tamid) of the afternoon and light the lamps in the evening.<br>And in Vayikra Rabbah (see Bemidbar Rabbah 12:15) I saw: Moses would set it up and disassemble it twice every day; Rabbi Chanina the Great says three times every day, as it is stated <i>\"תקים\"</i> (Exodus 40:2), <i>\"הוקם\"</i> (Exodus 40:17), <i>\"ויקם\"</i> (Exodus 40:18) — once for the morning tamid, once for the ordination, and once for the afternoon tamid. And it is possible that all this was the regular practice, to make known the matter of its erection and arrangement, and he would not leave it disassembled at all. And the verse that says here <i>\"ויכס הענן את אהל מועד וכבוד ה' מלא את המשכן\"</i> (Exodus 40:34) — according to their opinion this was on the eighth day, for it says <i>\"ויכל משה את המלאכה\"</i> (Exodus 40:33), and when he completed this erection of the first of Nisan, the cloud covered the Tabernacle. And Rashi has already written (Leviticus 9:23) what they expounded (Sifra ad loc.), <i>\"ויצאו ויברכו את העם\"</i> — because throughout the seven days of ordination during which Moses set up the Tabernacle and ministered in it and disassembled it, the Shekhinah did not rest upon it, and Israel were humiliated and said to Moses, \"Moses our teacher, all the trouble we undertook so that the Shekhinah would dwell among us and we would know that the sin of the calf was atoned for!\" He said to them, \"Aaron my brother is worthy and more distinguished than I, for through his offerings and his service the Shekhinah will dwell among us.\"<br>And in the section of the ordination (Sifra ad loc.): One might think the Tabernacle was set up on the new moon and the Shekhinah rested on the eighth of the month — Scripture teaches, saying <i>\"וביום הקים את המשכן כסה הענן את המשכן לאהל העדת\"</i> (Numbers 9:15), which teaches that on the day the Tabernacle was set up, the Shekhinah rested through the service of Aaron. Behold, they say explicitly that the cloud's covering of the Tabernacle was on the eighth day of ordination, and that is the first of Nisan. If so, this entire section is, according to their opinion, on the eighth day. And this was because Scripture arranges that HaShem commanded Moses that the erection of the Tabernacle should be completed on the first day of the first month, on the first of the month, and it says that Moses did so and completed all the work, and then the cloud covered the tent, and so always. And the verse returns to the beginning of the discourse that had been to Moses from the Tent and says <i>\"ויקרא אל משה\"</i> (Leviticus 1:1), and all this is in proper sequence.<br>And as a proof for them, similar to what is written (Numbers 7:1) <i>\"ויהי ביום כלות משה להקים את המשכן\"</i> — and if he did not take it down, why \"on the day of completing,\" for on a single day he began and completed, and it would be fitting to say <i>\"ויהי ביום הקים משה את המשכן\"</i>? And furthermore, it says there <i>\"זה הדבר אשר צוה ה' תעשו\"</i> (Leviticus 9:6), <i>\"וירא כבוד ה' אל כל העם\"</i> (Leviticus 9:23), and this implies that the cloud had not yet covered the Tent of Meeting and the glory of HaShem had not yet filled the Tabernacle. Nevertheless, on the first day of ordination Moses was addressed from there with all the sections stated from the beginning of the book of Leviticus until <i>\"ויהי ביום השמיני\"</i> (Leviticus 9:1), but the cloud did not cover it, and they assumed that the discourse to Moses came from heaven as it had been in the land of Egypt. But in the midrash of Rabbi Ishmael (on Ecclesiastes 1:12) I found: <i>\"ויהי ביום השמיני\"</i> — this should properly have been at the beginning of the book, so why was it written here? Because there is no earlier and later in the Torah. If so, <i>\"ויקרא אל משה מאהל מועד\"</i> would come after <i>\"וירא כבוד ה' אל כל העם ותצא אש ותאכל על המזבח\"</i> (Leviticus 9:23–24), and the discourse to Aaron <i>\"יין ושכר אל תשת\"</i> (Leviticus 10:9) would be from the next day, for it is impossible that Aaron was addressed from the Tent of Meeting before Moses. And I do not know whether this is the opinion of all or the opinion of an individual, for on the words of Rabbi Ishmael it is said there:" "<b>You shall set up the Tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting</b> — He did not explain to him in this command the order of erection as he explained it in the narrative, <i>\"ויתן את אדניו וישם את קרשיו\"</i> (Exodus 40:18). And this was because He had already shown him that erection in a prophetic vision, as He said <i>\"והקמת את המשכן כמשפטו אשר הראית בהר\"</i> (Exodus 26:30). And likewise He abbreviated here and said <i>\"ושמת שם את ארון העדת\"</i> (Exodus 40:3), and did not mention <i>ואל הארן תתן את העדת</i>, for by mentioning <i>\"את ארון העדת\"</i> he would understand this, since the Ark is not called thus except when the tablets of the testimony are in it. And he had already been commanded initially <i>\"ונתת את הכפרת על הארן מלמעלה ואל הארן תתן את העדת אשר אתן אליך\"</i> (Exodus 25:21), and there was no need here except to command him regarding precedence, for the placement of the Ark with the tablets precedes all the vessels. And likewise He abbreviated regarding the table and the menorah, for He had already commanded him (Exodus 26:35) in which part of the Tabernacle to place them. And He abbreviated regarding the garments of Aaron and his sons, saying <i>\"והלבשת את אהרן את בגדי הקדש\"</i> (Exodus 40:13), and regarding his sons He said <i>\"והלבשתם כתנת\"</i> (Exodus 40:14), for He had already commanded him in detail with the order of their donning (above 29:5–9), and now He came only to arrange for him the timing of the vesting, that it should be after the erection of the entire Tabernacle. And He mentioned the tunics, with which the vesting begins."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "Ramban cites the midrash halakhah known as Sifra de-Vei Rav (the school of Rabbi Ishmael) and notes its principle of ein mukdam u-me'uchar; he expresses uncertainty about the attribution."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:23:28.470648787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}